  ('bogner', 'Bogner', ARRAY['bogner','fire + ice','fire+ice']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops (body inches, US confection ↔ EU ↔ alpha)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','blouse','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','polo','cardigan']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS / US 4 / EU 34","measurements":{"bust":"31.5-32.7","waist":"25.2-26.4","hip":"34.6-35.8"}},{"size":"S / US 6 / EU 36","measurements":{"bust":"33.1-34.3","waist":"26.8-28","hip":"36.2-37.4"}},{"size":"M / US 8 / EU 38","measurements":{"bust":"34.6-35.8","waist":"28.3-29.5","hip":"37.8-39"}},{"size":"L / US 10 / EU 40","measurements":{"bust":"36.2-37.4","waist":"29.9-31.1","hip":"39.4-40.2"}},{"size":"XL / US 12 / EU 42","measurements":{"bust":"37.8-39","waist":"31.5-32.7","hip":"40.6-41.3"}},{"size":"XXL / US 14 / EU 44","measurements":{"bust":"39.4-40.9","waist":"33.1-34.6","hip":"41.7-43.3"}},{"size":"3XL / US 16 / EU 46","measurements":{"bust":"41.3-43.3","waist":"35-36.6","hip":"43.7-44.9"}},{"size":"4XL / US 18 / EU 48","measurements":{"bust":"43.7-45.7","waist":"37-39","hip":"45.3-46.9"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Bogner runs three labels at once — a US confection number, the EU number and a casual alpha — and its own chart prints all three against one body. A Bogner 38 is a US 8 and an M. It also publishes a LONG run (L4-L18, EU 68-96) with identical girths for a 68-71in height; that is a length class, not a different size.', 'https://www.bogner.com/en-us/size-guide/99.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('bogner', 'Bogner', ARRAY['bogner','fire + ice','fire+ice']::text[], 'Men', 'Tops (body inches, US confection ↔ EU ↔ alpha)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','polo','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','cardigan']::text[], $json$[{"size":"S / US 36 / EU 46","measurements":{"chest":"35.4-36.6","waist":"30.7-31.9"}},{"size":"M / US 38 / EU 48","measurements":{"chest":"37-38.2","waist":"32.3-33.5"}},{"size":"L / US 40 / EU 50","measurements":{"chest":"38.6-39.8","waist":"33.9-35"}},{"size":"XL / US 42 / EU 52","measurements":{"chest":"40.2-41.3","waist":"35.4-37"}},{"size":"XXL / US 44 / EU 54","measurements":{"chest":"41.7-42.9","waist":"37-39"}},{"size":"3XL / US 46 / EU 56","measurements":{"chest":"43.3-44.5","waist":"39.4-41.3"}},{"size":"4XL / US 48 / EU 58","measurements":{"chest":"44.9-46.1","waist":"41.7-43.7"}},{"size":"5XL / US 50 / EU 60","measurements":{"chest":"46.5-47.6","waist":"44.1-46.1"}},{"size":"6XL / US 52 / EU 62","measurements":{"chest":"48-49.2","waist":"46.5-48"}},{"size":"7XL / US 54 / EU 64","measurements":{"chest":"49.6-50.8","waist":"48.4-50"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Bogner''s men''s chart, three labels against one body: a Bogner 50 is an EU 50 and an L. The alpha run goes all the way to 7XL, which is unusual and is the brand''s own. Bogner also prints a separate SHIRT chart in HALF chest, which is a garment measurement and is not this chart.', 'https://www.bogner.com/en-us/size-guide/99.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('bonobos', 'Bonobos', ARRAY['bonobos']::text[], 'Men', 'Shirts, standard fit (GARMENT inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','polo','button','oxford']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"38","length":"28.75","sleeve":"32.25"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"41","length":"29.375","sleeve":"33.5"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"44","length":"30","sleeve":"34.75"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"47","length":"30.625","sleeve":"35.5"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"50","length":"31.25","sleeve":"36.25"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"53","length":"31.875","sleeve":"37"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'THE FIRST CHART IN THIS CORPUS THAT IS FLAT RATHER THAN BODY, and it is flat because Bonobos says so above its own table: ''Measurements reflect garment dimensions. All units are in inches.'' Do not add ease to these. This is the STANDARD fit; Bonobos steps the chest 1in per fit — Slim is 1in narrower, Tailored 2in — and leaves body length and sleeve alone. Short shirts are 1.25in shorter in body and 2in in sleeve; long shirts are 1.5in longer in both.', 'https://bonobos.com/products/stretch-washed-button-down-shirt', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('bonobos', 'Bonobos', ARRAY['bonobos']::text[], 'Men', 'Outerwear (GARMENT inches)', ARRAY['jacket','coat','outerwear','parka','vest','bomber']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"40.5","length":"26.75","sleeve":"34"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"43.5","length":"27.375","sleeve":"34.75"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"46.5","length":"28","sleeve":"35.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"49.5","length":"28.625","sleeve":"36.25"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"52.5","length":"29.25","sleeve":"37"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"55.5","length":"29.875","sleeve":"37.75"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Bonobos outerwear comes in one fit and, like its shirts, the numbers are GARMENT dimensions rather than body. The chest runs 3in per size against the shirts'' 3in but starts 2.5in wider, which is the allowance for what goes under it.', 'https://bonobos.com/products/fairgame-filled-jacket', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('brooksbrothers', 'Brooks Brothers', ARRAY['brooks brothers','brooksbrothers']::text[], 'Men', 'Bottoms (body inches)', ARRAY['bottom','pant','trouser','short','chino','jean']::text[], $json$[{"size":"28 (XS)","measurements":{"waist":"28.5","hip":"36"}},{"size":"29","measurements":{"waist":"29.5","hip":"37"}},{"size":"30 (S)","measurements":{"waist":"30.5","hip":"38"}},{"size":"31","measurements":{"waist":"31.5","hip":"39"}},{"size":"32","measurements":{"waist":"32.5","hip":"40"}},{"size":"33 (M)","measurements":{"waist":"33.5","hip":"41"}},{"size":"34","measurements":{"waist":"34.5","hip":"42"}},{"size":"35","measurements":{"waist":"35.5","hip":"43"}},{"size":"36","measurements":{"waist":"36.5","hip":"44"}},{"size":"37 (L)","measurements":{"waist":"37.5","hip":"45"}},{"size":"38","measurements":{"waist":"38.5","hip":"46"}},{"size":"39","measurements":{"waist":"39.5","hip":"47"}},{"size":"40","measurements":{"waist":"40.5","hip":"48"}},{"size":"42 (XL)","measurements":{"waist":"42.5","hip":"50"}},{"size":"44","measurements":{"waist":"44.5","hip":"52"}},{"size":"46 (XXL)","measurements":{"waist":"46.5","hip":"54"}},{"size":"48","measurements":{"waist":"48.5","hip":"56"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Brooks Brothers'' men''s bottoms chart, with an alpha column beside the numeric waist. The tag number sits half an inch under the body waist all the way up, and the run is dense — every inch from 28 to 40 — so the alpha only lands on some of them.', 'https://www.brooksbrothers.com/sizeguide?cid=men-casual-pants', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('brooksbrothers', 'Brooks Brothers', ARRAY['brooks brothers','brooksbrothers']::text[], 'Men', 'Bottoms, big (body inches)', ARRAY['bottom','pant','trouser','short','chino']::text[], $json$[{"size":"36 (LB)","measurements":{"waist":"38","hip":"44.5"}},{"size":"38","measurements":{"waist":"40","hip":"46.5"}},{"size":"40","measurements":{"waist":"42","hip":"48.5"}},{"size":"42 (XLB)","measurements":{"waist":"44","hip":"50.5"}},{"size":"44","measurements":{"waist":"46","hip":"52.5"}},{"size":"46 (XXLB)","measurements":{"waist":"48","hip":"54.5"}},{"size":"48","measurements":{"waist":"50","hip":"56.5"}},{"size":"50 (2XLB)","measurements":{"waist":"52","hip":"58.5"}},{"size":"52","measurements":{"waist":"54","hip":"60.5"}},{"size":"54 (3XLB)","measurements":{"waist":"56","hip":"62.5"}},{"size":"56","measurements":{"waist":"58","hip":"64.5"}},{"size":"58","measurements":{"waist":"60","hip":"66.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Brooks Brothers'' BIG run, printed as its own table. The same tag number means a different body here: a 42 in the regular run fits a 42.5in waist and a 42 XLB fits a 44in one, so the two tables must not be read across.', 'https://www.brooksbrothers.com/sizeguide?cid=men-casual-pants', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('dickies', 'Dickies', ARRAY['dickies']::text[], 'Men', 'Tops & outerwear (body inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','polo','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','jacket','coat','outerwear','vest','coverall']::text[], $json$[{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"34-37","neck":"14.5","sleeve":"32.25"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"38-41","neck":"15.5","sleeve":"33.5"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"42-45","neck":"16.5","sleeve":"34.25"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"46-49","neck":"17.5","sleeve":"35"}},{"size":"2XL","measurements":{"chest":"50-53","neck":"18.5","sleeve":"35.75"}},{"size":"3XL","measurements":{"chest":"54-57","neck":"19.5","sleeve":"36.5"}},{"size":"4XL","measurements":{"chest":"58-60","neck":"20.5","sleeve":"37"}},{"size":"5XL","measurements":{"chest":"61-63","neck":"21.5","sleeve":"37.5"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Dickies publishes no outerwear chart — /pages/mens-outerwear-size-chart 404s — so its tops chart is the brand''s answer for work jackets too. Body measurements, and the run goes to 5XL, which matters for workwear more than for most brands in this corpus.', 'https://www.dickies.com/en-us/pages/mens-tops-size-chart', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('diesel', 'Diesel', ARRAY['diesel']::text[], 'Men', 'Tops (body inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','polo','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','cardigan']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"chest":"30-32","shoulder":"35-37"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"chest":"32-34","shoulder":"37-39"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"chest":"34-36","shoulder":"39-41"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"chest":"36-38","shoulder":"42-43"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"chest":"38-40","shoulder":"44-46"}},{"size":"XL","measurements":{"chest":"40-42","shoulder":"46-48"}},{"size":"XXL","measurements":{"chest":"43-44","shoulder":"48-51"}},{"size":"3XL","measurements":{"chest":"45-47","shoulder":"52-54"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Diesel''s men''s body chart, shoulders and chest. It also prints a country conversion in the same modal (XS = IT 42, XL = IT 52) where the alpha labels STRADDLE two Italian numbers, so a Diesel M is an IT 46 or 48 depending on the garment.', 'https://diesel.com/en-us/outerwear-%26-jackets/d-kraps-s-blue/A22619007EV01.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781'),
  ('diesel', 'Diesel', ARRAY['diesel']::text[], 'Women', 'Tops (body inches)', ARRAY['top','tee','shirt','blouse','sweater','knit','hoodie','sweatshirt','tank','cardigan']::text[], $json$[{"size":"XXS","measurements":{"bust":"30-31","shoulder":"35-36"}},{"size":"XS","measurements":{"bust":"31-33","shoulder":"36-37"}},{"size":"S","measurements":{"bust":"33-34","shoulder":"38-39"}},{"size":"M","measurements":{"bust":"35-36","shoulder":"39-41"}},{"size":"L","measurements":{"bust":"37-38","shoulder":"41-43"}}]$json$::jsonb, 'Diesel''s women''s body chart, shoulders and breast. ⚠ ITS XL ROW IS LEFT OUT ON PURPOSE: Diesel prints shoulders 39in and breast 43in there, which reverses the relationship every row above it has, so the two columns are transposed and there is no honest way to tell which value belongs where. The conversion in the same modal runs XXS = IT 34-36 through XL = IT 46-48, with the alpha labels straddling two Italian numbers.', 'https://diesel.com/en-us/t-shirts/t-ila-aa1-grey/A232400PLBQ77F.html', 0.85, false, 'migration:00781')
